From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] input: qcom-hv-haptics: stop playback when an effect is stopped

haptics_playback() only handled a start request. A stop request
(EV_FF with value 0) returned without touching the hardware, so an
effect kept playing until its replay.length timer fired. Clients that
open the haptics input device directly and stop rumble with
EVIOCSFF + EV_FF 0, such as SDL_HapticRumbleStop(), felt every short
rumble for the full requested length (5 s in sm64coopdx).

Run the existing stop worker immediately on a stop request while the
chip is playing. Stopping sleeps on SPMI and in the brake wait, and
playback can be called under the input device event_lock, so the stop
is deferred to the worker instead of being done inline.

--- a/drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c	2026-11-05 10:39:31.532775325 -0600
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c	2026-11-05 10:39:31.540914311 -0600
@@ -3383,6 +3383,10 @@
 		return haptics_enable_play(chip, true);
 	}
 
+	/* Stopping sleeps on SPMI; playback can run under the input event_lock. */
+	if (!val && chip->chip_is_playing)
+		mod_delayed_work(system_wq, &chip->stop_work, 0);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
